"‖", "claim": "Arrived Bremerhaven (11 Jun)", "citation": "Hubbard & Winter, North Atlantic Mail Sailings 1840-75 (USPCS, 1988; rev. 2014), p. 292", "source_kind": "compiled", "displayable": false, "crop": null, "verbatim": null, "lineage_id": "hw:nal-302-007-e:2", "source": "hw"}, {"mark": "¶", "claim": "Spoken / sighted lat\n42[?], lon 60[?] (26th[?])", "citation": "New York Herald, 30 May 1866, p. 5, col. 5", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866053001:1371/3632,7570,935,490/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship Persia (Br), Lott, Liverpool May 19, via Queens-\ntown 20th, with mdse and 199[?] passengers, to E Cunard. 19th[?]\ninst, off Tuskar, passed steamship Africa, from Boston, for\nLiverpool; same day, off Queenstown, bark Eddystone (Br);\n25th, lat 43[?], lon 44[?], bark Maxwell (Br), bound E; 26th[?], lat\n42[?], lon 60[?], steamship Ericsson, hence for Bremen; 27th[?], lat\n41[?], lon 69[?], ship Charlotte (Brem), bound W; 29th[?], 2 PM, off\nFire Island, ship Queen Pearl, bound W.", "lineage_id": "herald:L278a48cbc2f1d35e", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-30/ed-1/seq-5/"}, {"mark": "7", "claim": "Spoken / sighted in lat. 49 27, long. 27 03 (June 3)", "citation": "New-York Tribune, 13 June 1866, p. 7, col. 2", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_delphi_ver03:data:sn83030214:00206530832:1866061301:0309/1026,3188,1060,371/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "June 3, in lat. 49 27, long. 27 03, steamships Ericsson, Bavaria, and\na Glasgow steamer, bound E.", "lineage_id": "tribune:L34df2935402ad608", "source": "tribune", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030214/1866-06-13/ed-1/seq-7/"}, {"mark": "8", "claim": "Spoken / sighted in lat. 42 N, long. 60 W (May 27)", "citation": "New-York Tribune, 30 May 1866, p. 6, col. 6", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_delphi_ver03:data:sn83030214:00206530832:1866053001:0212/4994,6397,1039,194/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "The Persia at this port, from Liverpool, reports having passed vessels\nas follows: May 20, off Tuskar, Company's steamship Africa, bound\nto Liverpool; May 20, off Queenstown, British bark Eddystone; May\n25, in lat. 43 N, long. 44 W, Br. bark \"Maxwell,\" bound W; May 27,\nin lat. 42 N, long. 60 W, Am. steamship Ericsson, bound E; May 28,\nin lat. 41, long. 60, Bremen ship Charlotte, bound W.", "lineage_id": "tribune:L696da14bd14acc39", "source": "tribune", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030214/1866-05-30/ed-1/seq-6/"}, {"mark": "9", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-05-23)", "citation": "New York Herald, 24 May 1866, p. 5, col. 5", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_goldenglow_ver01:data:sn83030313:00271743543:1866052401:1317/3660,4207,947,340/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship Ericsson, Lowber, Bremen via Cowes—Ruger\nBros.", "lineage_id": "herald:L2aca30b7edcb8324", "source": "herald", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030313/1866-05-24/ed-1/seq-5/"}, {"mark": "10", "claim": "Cleared New York (1866-05-23)", "citation": "New-York Tribune, 24 May 1866, p. 7, col. 1", "source_kind": "newspaper", "displayable": true, "crop": "https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:ndnp:dlc:batch_dlc_delphi_ver03:data:sn83030214:00206530832:1866052401:0173/72,7753,1042,120/640,/0/default.jpg", "verbatim": "Steamship Ericsson, Lowber, Bremen via Cowes, Ruger Bros.", "lineage_id": "tribune:L4cd9fc864ead99ee", "source": "tribune", "url": "https://chroniclingamerica.loc.gov/lccn/sn83030214/1866-05-24/ed-1/seq-7/"}], "aboard": {"specie": [], "passenge